  "note": "Triennial election of the Kilkeel Urban District Council (nine members, whole town), due 15 May 1939; nine nominations for nine seats, so there was no poll. Nine outgoing members returned unopposed; Mr. M'Gonigle was chairman of the outgoing council. The News-Letter (6 May 1939, p. 9) printed only eight names and has 'James J. Fagan' for the Frontier Sentinel's 'J. J. Fegan'. Returned unopposed."
